 - [ ] **REG-002**: When a lookup completes, the system SHALL include the active snapshot date in the result.
 - [ ] **REG-003**: When a snapshot has an invalid signature, an unsupported schema version, or duplicate serial numbers, the system SHALL reject the import and retain the active snapshot.
 - [ ] **REG-004**: When a valid replacement snapshot is activated, the system SHALL expose all of its records together without exposing a partially imported snapshot.
+- [ ] **REG-005**: When a validated snapshot is imported, the system SHALL build a new SQLite database file containing all records with a primary key on serial_number before activating it.
+- [ ] **REG-006**: When the active snapshot pointer is swapped, the system SHALL perform the swap atomically so that concurrent lookups see either the old or the new snapshot, never a partial state.
+- [ ] **REG-007**: When a lookup executes, the system SHALL query the SQLite index using a prepared statement with a bound parameter and return Found or NotFound within 250 ms.
+- [ ] **REG-008**: When a snapshot import fails at any stage, the system SHALL leave the previous snapshot's database file and active pointer unchanged and report a useful error.
